@page "/getting-started"

<PageTitle>Getting Started | BookHeaven</PageTitle>
<section class="max-w-[700px]">
	<p class="font-bold text-4xl md:text-6xl mb-10 text-white">
		Getting Started with <span class="text-(--color-primary)">BookHeaven</span>
	</p>
	<p class="italic text-balance text-white">Follow the steps below to get your digital library up and running in no time.</p>
</section>
<hr class="my-5 md:my-10 text-neutral-700"/>
<section class="flex flex-col gap-5">
	<h1 class="text-(--color-primary) font-bold text-4xl mb-3">Server</h1>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Requirements</h2>
	<ul class="list-disc ms-5">
		<li><a href="https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/" target="_blank">Docker</a> or <a href="https://podman.io/docs/installation" target="_blank">Podman</a></li>
	</ul>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Step 1 - Prepare and spin up your container</h2>
	<h3 class="text-xl">- Docker Compose</h3>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		Create a <code>compose.yml</code> file with the following content, making sure to customize it to your desired values:
	</p>
	<pre>
		<code class="language-yaml">services:
  bookheaven:
    image: ghcr.io/bookheaven/bookheaven-server:latest
    container_name: bookheaven
    volumes:
      # point the /app/data path to a persistent location on your host
      # this is where all your books, covers, fonts, etc will be stored
      # make sure the user running the container down below has read and write permissions to this folder
      - ./data:/app/data
      # optional: if you want to import books by copying them directly into a folder on your host
      - ./import:/app/import
    ports:
      # web ui
      - 8080:8080
      # optional: required for auto discovery, changing the default port is not supported for now since it's hardcoded in the client
      - 27007:27007/udp
    environment:
      # optional: required for auto discovery, change to your desired domain or ip:port, including the protocol (http or https)
      - SERVER_URL=https://bookheaven.yourdomain.tld
      - TZ=Europe/Madrid
    user: 1000:1000
    restart: unless-stopped</code>
	</pre>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		Then run the following command in the same folder where you created the <code>compose.yml</code> file:
	</p>
	<pre>
		<code class="language-bash">docker compose up -d</code>
	</pre>
	<h3 class="text-xl">- Docker Run</h3>
	<pre>
		<code class="language-bash">docker run -d --name bookheaven --user 1000:1000 \
  -p 8080:8080 -p 27007:27007/udp \
  -v $PWD/data:/app/data \
  -v $PWD/import:/app/import \
  -e SERVER_URL=https://bookheaven.yourdomain.tld \
  ghcr.io/bookheaven/bookheaven-server:latest</code>
	</pre>
	<h3 class="text-xl">- Podman</h3>
	<pre>
		<code class="language-bash">podman run -d --name bookheaven --userns=keep-id \
  -p 8080:8080 -p 27007:27007/udp \
  -v $PWD/data:/app/data:Z,U \
  -v $PWD/import:/app/import:Z,U \
  -e SERVER_URL=https://bookheaven.yourdomain.tld \
  ghcr.io/bookheaven/bookheaven-server:latest</code>
	</pre>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Step 2 - Create your first profile</h2>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		Open your browser and go to <code>@("http://<your-server-ip>:8080")</code>. You will be greeted by the profile selection screen prompting you to create your first profile.<br/>
		Just click on the big "+" button, fill in your desired name and click save.<br/>
	</p>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Step 3 - Start uploading books</h2>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		Once inside the app, click on the upload button, located next to the search bar in the top right corner of the screen, to add your first book.<br/>
		You could also add your books by copying them directly into the <code>/import</code> folder you created in step 1.<br/>
		The server will read the metadata from the books and organize them into authors and series automatically and you can edit them at any time if you want.<br/>
	</p>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Final Notes</h2>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		I recommend you to use a reverse proxy in front of your Server to enable HTTPS and add a layer of security, but also because otherwise the Reader app might not be able to see the covers until it downloads the books, since it requires a secure connection to fetch them.<br/>
	</p>
</section>
<hr class="my-5 md:my-10 text-neutral-700"/>
<section class="flex flex-col gap-5">
	<h1 class="text-(--color-primary) font-bold text-4xl mb-3">Reader</h1>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Requirements</h2>
	<ul class="list-disc ms-5">
		<li>Android 10+</li>
		<li class="italic">It MIGHT work on Android 8+ if you can update the webview to version 138.0.7204.181, which is the highest supported I could find. No promises.</li>
	</ul>
	<span class="px-3 py-2 bg-yellow-800 border border-yellow-500 rounded">Please make sure your Android System Webview is up to date to avoid any issues. You might need to update it manually. Check out the troubleshooting section on <a href="https://github.com/BookHeaven/BookHeaven.reader" target="_blank">the readme</a> for more info.</span>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Step 1 - Download and install the app</h2>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		You can download the app manually from the <a href="https://github.com/BookHeaven/BookHeaven.Reader/releases" target="_blank">main repository</a>, or you can use <a href="https://obtainium.imranr.dev/" target="_blank">Obtainium</a> which I highly recommend, since it will notify you when a new version is available and allow you to easily update it.<br/>
		I won't be explaining here how Obtainium works, but it's really easy to use and you can find more information on their website.<br/>
	</p>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Step 2 - Go through the setup process</h2>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		Activate your Wi-Fi and launch the app.<br/>
		When you open the app for the first time, you will be greeted by a setup wizard that will guide you through the process of connecting to your server.<br/>
		If you have auto discovery enabled, the app should configure itself automatically, otherwise you will have to enter the server URL manually.<br/>
		Once connected, you will be able to see the profiles you created in the server and select the one you want to use.<br/>
		You can always change the active profile later.<br/>
	</p>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Step 3 - Start downloading and reading books</h2>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		Once inside the app, you will see and empty library and a button prompting you to download some books. So, click on it.<br/>
		You will be able to see all the books available in the server, and you can download them by clicking on the download button on each book.<br/>
		Once downloaded, you can read them by clicking on the book cover.<br/>
		To customize your reading experience, you can open the overlay by tapping in the middle of the screen while a book is opened.<br/>
		Have fun discovering how many options are available to you to make reading as comfortable as possible!<br/>
	</p>
	<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Final Notes</h2>
	<p class="text-slate-300">
		The app is designed to work offline, so you can read your books without an internet connection.<br/>
		You can sync your progress manually by taping on the three dot button in the top right corner of the home screen.<br/>
	</p>
</section>

@code {
	[Inject] private IJSRuntime JsRuntime { get; set; } = null!;
	protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
	{
		if(firstRender) await JsRuntime.InvokeVoidAsync("Prism.highlightAll");
	}

}